  "question": {
    "text": "If $n={ }^m C_2$, then the value of ${ }^n C_2$ is given by",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "8ZR1d",
      "text": "\n$3\\left({ }^{m+1} C_4\\right)$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "psHX2",
      "text": "\n${ }^{m-1} C_4$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "0HM0w",
      "text": "\n${ }^{m+1} C_4$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "xoOmc",
      "text": "\n$2\\left({ }^{m+2} C_4\\right)$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$n={ }^m \\mathrm{C}_2=\\frac{m(m-1)}{2}$\nSince $m$ and $(m-1)$ are two consecutive natural numbers, therefore their product is an even natural number. So $\\frac{m(m-1)}{2}$ is also a natural number.\nNow $\\frac{m(m-1)}{2}=\\frac{m^2-m}{2}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\therefore & \\frac{m(m-1)}{2} \\mathrm{C}_2=\\frac{\\left(\\frac{m^2-m}{2}\\right)\\left(\\frac{m^2-m}{2}-1\\right)}{2} \\\\\n& =\\frac{m(m-1)\\left(m^2-m-2\\right)}{8} \\\\\n& =\\frac{m(m-1)\\left[m^2-2 m+m-2\\right]}{8} \\\\\n& =\\frac{m(m-1)[m(m-2)+1(m-2)]}{8} \\\\\n& =\\frac{m(m-1)(m-2)(m+1)}{8}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/GmFZabZ9BxLMTQm8_bjMZITikozczSvtWUeTCPXDhFE.original.fullsize.png\"><br>",
    "image": null
